 ### Priority
 
@@ -118,15 +123,31 @@ ### Ordering and Fairness
 
 The **next candidate queue** is **deterministic**: same state input → same next ticket, no random draw.
 
+**Implementation (`App\Actions\CallNextTicket`, invoked as `(new CallNextTicket)($queue, $user, $mode)`):**
+
+- **Ordering:** higher `priority` first, then oldest `issued_at`, then lowest `id`.
+- **Candidates:** only `waiting` tickets of the given queue. A ticket that is already called is never called again.
+- **Modes** (`App\Enums\CallMode`):
+  - `any`: full ordering, plus the fairness rule.
+  - `priority_only`: priority tickets only (`priority > 0`), full ordering, fairness ignored.
+  - `normal_only`: normal tickets only (`priority = 0`), oldest first, fairness ignored.
+- **Fairness (`any` only):** look at the last 3 tickets called in the queue, most recent first by `called_at` then `id`. If there are 3, all are priority tickets, and a normal ticket is waiting, the call is restricted to the oldest normal ticket. Calls made in any mode count towards the streak, and a normal call resets it. If no normal ticket is waiting, priority tickets keep being called.
+- **Timestamp precision:** `called_at` has second precision. Calls made within the same second tie on `called_at`, so the fairness window orders them by `id`, not by call time.
+- **Inactive queue:** the queue row is locked and `is_active` is read from the database (never from the passed instance). Calling from an inactive queue throws `InactiveQueueException` and changes nothing.
+- **No eligible ticket:** an empty queue, only normal tickets in `priority_only`, or only priority tickets in `normal_only` throws `NoWaitingTicketsException` and changes nothing.
+- **Exactly once:** the chosen ticket's row is locked and its status re-checked as `waiting`. If it was called in the meantime (for example through `Ticket::call()`), it is skipped and the next candidate is selected.
+- **Result:** the winner gets `status=called`, `called_at = now()`, and `called_by_user_id`. The updated model is returned. Only those three fields change (write-once rule).
+- **Authorization:** who may call is not checked by this action. The caller (HTTP or Livewire layer) must authorize before calling it.
+
 ### Call Panel (attendant)
 
 Three explicit actions, all deterministic:
 
-| Button | Behavior |
-| ----- | ------------- |
-| **Next (most important)** | Calls the next ticket according to full ordering (priority + age + 3-ticket fairness rule). |
-| **Priority** | Calls the next eligible ticket **only** among priority candidates (includes 80+ per configuration). |
-| **Normal** | Calls the next eligible ticket **only** among normal candidates. |
+| Button | Behavior | `CallMode` |
+| ----- | ------------- | ----- |
+| **Next (most important)** | Calls the next ticket according to full ordering (priority + age + 3-ticket fairness rule). | `any` |
+| **Priority** | Calls the next eligible ticket **only** among priority candidates (includes 80+ per configuration). | `priority_only` |
+| **Normal** | Calls the next eligible ticket **only** among normal candidates. | `normal_only` |
 
 After each call, the ticket leaves the waiting queue and enters the session/display call history.
 
